	(text_box "U10/L2 boosts voltage until feedback pin limits to ~15mA by 13.3ohm resistor\nLED_SW high voltage pin can control up to 29V output, after that shuts down with built-in OVP\nWhen active, positive voltage travel to either warm LED strip or cool LED strip (W+/C+)\nCircuit completes to either depending on COLOR_SEL polarity via GPIO\nBrightness controlled by PWM duty cycle on CTRL pin\nEntire circuit can be toggled via LED_ACTIVATE GPIO (active low)\nIf circuit is left open (no LED strip connected) then the voltage on SW/inductor will climb over 29V OVP threshold and shutdown\nBefore that can trip, conditions over 22V will trip path from D9 and de-latch LED_ACTIVATE GPIO, an open-drain pin\nLatched safety condition draws a lot of unfortunate idle current (about 9mA in simulation), so software will need to ensure that its pin toggles itself semi-regularly"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 259.08 344.17 0)
		(size 119.38 24.13)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d9776652-e2cb-4ef8-bff8-aa74367099da")
	)
